{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T13:07:48.604Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1c7226cdcb831e4341d98ac7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-e3hfv8","claim:pm-fkhdy8","claim:pm-rrwh2o","claim:pm-sbqn4h","lineage:pm-sbqn4h","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-e3hfv8+pm-fkhdy8+pm-rrwh2o+pm-sbqn4h","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-e3hfv8","claim:pm-fkhdy8","claim:pm-rrwh2o","claim:pm-sbqn4h","lineage:pm-sbqn4h","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T13:07:48.604Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-08T13:07:48.603Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implementation evidence, branch fix/annotation-read-fidelity. validateReadOutputOptions now throws readOutputMutationConflict. Fields: code read_output_mutation_conflict (exit 2, catalogued in generated-error-code-catalog-part-2.ts and listed in docs/generated/REFUSAL_CLOSURE_CENSUS.md); field (the first control); details.surface; details.output_controls (CLI flags); details.output_option_keys (the camelCase or snake_case keys the SDK or MCP caller supplied); details.mutation_options; a required line that says to retry without the controls and read with them separately; and runnable per-surface examples. HYBRID_READ_MUTATION_KEYS is now typed over exactly the six hybrid surfaces, so every surface has examples and no unreachable fallback exists. CLI: src/cli/runtime/read-output-mutation-retry.ts rewrites the recovery as the caller's argv without each control token and the value it consumed. It is wired into repairInvocationRecovery in main.ts beside the other mutation retries and binds an environment-selected tracker the same way. Flag arity comes from scanOptionTokens in projection-retry.ts, which now reports each token's consumed value, so arity has one source. The error path records argv as 'item comments ...', so the repair resolves the two-token command path before scanning. Verified with the built CLI: 'pm learnings <id> --add x --output-limit 3 --output-cursor=abc --output-row-contract --json' exits 2 with suggested_retry 'pm item learnings <id> --add x --json', and that retry runs. MCP tools/call returns the code, details and output_option_keys."}]}],"before_hash":"6f6b82618c7e76c1a1c96337d26e462919cec81ff8499cc5fc21faa0452fbe0e","after_hash":"b260abbe2b3e98077364ae0e63eb1cafc6a80dd87e1090d7c1c6015abf291017","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b12814ade34ea582158ac5a907777e64e1af8a10880638d43b14fbb86499553c"}
