{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T13:44:55.236Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1c7226cdcb831e4341d98ac7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-e3hfv8","claim:pm-fkhdy8","claim:pm-rrwh2o","claim:pm-sbqn4h","lineage:pm-sbqn4h","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-e3hfv8+pm-fkhdy8+pm-rrwh2o+pm-sbqn4h","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-e3hfv8","claim:pm-fkhdy8","claim:pm-rrwh2o","claim:pm-sbqn4h","lineage:pm-sbqn4h","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"close","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"pm learnings <id> --add x --output-limit 3 --json exits 2 with code read_output_mutation_conflict, details.output_controls [--output-limit] and suggested_retry_args without the control; the retry runs; MCP tools/call returns the code with output_option_keys"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"The refusal carries a stable typed code, names the offending output flags, and suggests a retry of the mutation without them through CLI, SDK and MCP"},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/claim_principal"},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/assignee"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T13:44:55.236Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/status","value":"closed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/closed_at","value":"2026-11-08T13:44:55.153Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/completed_at","value":"2026-11-08T13:44:55.153Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/resolution","value":"validateReadOutputOptions throws read_output_mutation_conflict, exit 2, catalogued and listed in the refusal-closure census. It carries details.output_controls (the CLI flags), details.output_option_keys (the keys an SDK or MCP caller supplied), details.mutation_options, a required line and runnable per-surface examples. src/cli/runtime/read-output-mutation-retry.ts rewrites the CLI recovery as the caller's argv without each control and the value it consumed. Arity comes from scanOptionTokens in projection-retry.ts, and namespaced command paths resolve. The repair binds an environment-selected tracker like the other mutation retries. READ_OUTPUT_MUTATION_CONFLICT_CODE and READ_OUTPUT_SHAPING_CONTROL_FLAGS are exported."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/close_reason","value":"Fixed: a mutation given universal output controls is refused with the typed code read_output_mutation_conflict and a retry without them"}],"before_hash":"dbcab4a17048b6b82402203e47d0664c574977f69d818a8409a73fc3b1302a13","after_hash":"aa2394cce71846cd9735538b6b36a9adc684554e50058b717167985f43bfb4c9","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"completion":{"timestamp":"2026-11-08T13:44:55.153Z","source":"close_time"},"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"3ec5bfcf4abfd42f2ee1cd663d7f1e063f4142d1690738413168c7e9b20b8f02"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T13:45:05.490Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1c7226cdcb831e4341d98ac7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"release-operator","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-rrwh2o","claim:pm-sbqn4h","release:pm-fkhdy8"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-rrwh2o+pm-sbqn4h","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-rrwh2o","claim:pm-sbqn4h","release:pm-fkhdy8"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"release","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T13:45:05.490Z"}],"before_hash":"aa2394cce71846cd9735538b6b36a9adc684554e50058b717167985f43bfb4c9","after_hash":"6c418be7214927d70b9023608ba62a5e06c255ee48af7343524c4a26a784425d","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"maintenance","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ca665f83fc4c217b12e3eac6e0b688dc139c41185a110925fbc717ba9a36106f"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T14:21:01.482Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1c7226cdcb831e4341d98ac7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-08T14:21:01.481Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review fix on PR 1688 (Codex P1 and Greptile P2). The retry scanner reads value arity from vocabulary rows, which leave command flags such as --message untyped. Global normalization also lets a value-taking control swallow the next option: in 'comments pm-one --add kept --message --output-limit --pm-path /tmp/A --output-budget 500', --output-limit takes --pm-path as its value and the tracker path becomes the --message text. The rebuilt retry 'comments pm-one --add kept --message /tmp/A' was faithful to that parse, but it replayed the misparse as a clean write to the environment tracker. repairReadOutputMutationRecovery now withholds the retry in two cases. First, when a control consumed a flag-like token. Second, when a control directly follows a value-taking option, using the arity from enrichCliFlagInvocationContracts, which the flag-invocation parity gate verifies against the parser. In both cases the refusal still names the controls to drop. Specs cover the Codex argv, the dash-led budget case, the Greptile argv, '--add --output-limit', inline and boolean predecessors, a control before the command and a trailing control. A two-tracker CLI regression asserts that no retry is suggested and nothing is written. Measured on the built CLI: '--message --foo-bar' stores the message '--foo-bar', while '--message --pm-path X' and '--message --output-limit 2' are refused as an argument missing before any read-output refusal."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T14:21:01.482Z"}],"before_hash":"6c418be7214927d70b9023608ba62a5e06c255ee48af7343524c4a26a784425d","after_hash":"a9188079f464a886e1a5e57cf689c06644ae1147413161ea47628e7c84a02736","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ff213ec79bd0c9383e64a2b731e86d00a4b8e7deed27e2d41684826eea026dcf"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T14:41:08.770Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1c7226cdcb831e4341d98ac7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-08T14:41:08.769Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"CodeRabbit review of PR 1688, two findings declined with reasons. (1) The direct SDK runComments write with outputInclude in its global options: direct SDK primitives never apply universal output controls. A direct runComments read with outputLimit 1 still returns three rows. Shaping is a delivery-layer contract of the CLI and runAction, and runAction (the SDK and MCP transport) refuses the combination with read_output_mutation_conflict. Refusing direct writes would make writes stricter than reads at the same layer. (2) 'pm files discover <id> --apply --output-limit 3' gets the typed refusal but no suggested retry, because no contract source declares --apply: pm contracts --command 'files discover' is unknown_command. Withholding is the designed safe outcome. The contract gap is filed as pm-9ke7h9. A third finding, projection-retry arity for the search-advanced package's --for, concerns the pre-existing projection retry; this PR only moved that scanner, and an ambiguous argv already withholds the retry there."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T14:41:08.770Z"}],"before_hash":"a9188079f464a886e1a5e57cf689c06644ae1147413161ea47628e7c84a02736","after_hash":"ed4d4f373dc90793915e9eacc105d7bd87585a7e86e451539174d4ef99a39b2a","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a45898f856e965be5cbd4a7a098f9f34047ee98268ea9bb0a3ccc398f8020915"}
